From: ksre-ps5
Subject: timemodule: test the value of HAVE_DECL_TZNAME, not only whether it is defined

AC_CHECK_DECLS defines HAVE_DECL_TZNAME to 0 when tzname is not declared, but
timemodule.c tests it with #ifdef/#ifndef, so "not declared" selects the tzname
path. configure only runs that check when struct tm has no tm_zone, which is
the PS5 case: the SDK's struct tm declares tm_zone/tm_gmtoff, but the console
libc's localtime_s() does not fill them, so config.site turns tm_zone off and
also answers tzname=no (the FreeBSD headers declare timezone() as a function).
With this change init_timezone() uses the localtime()/strftime("%Z")/timegm()
path, as intended for platforms without tzname.

